From: WelsonJS
Subject: [PATCH] model : support EmbeddingGemma 2 (gemma-embedding2), text encoder

Support the text encoder of google/embeddinggemma-2 (Apache-2.0), the
architecture "gemma-embedding2" of its GGUF files (for example
ggml-org/embeddinggemma-2-GGUF), so the WelsonJS build serves its embeddings
(llama-server --embedding). The fork predates the upstream support.

Backport of the C++ part of upstream llama.cpp 4fbc76dec5 ("model: support
embeddinggemma2 (text+vision+audio)", ggml-org/llama.cpp#30054, MIT). The
vision and audio encoders (mmproj) and the Python conversion are not part of
it; the GGUF files are converted upstream.

1. Register the architecture: LLM_ARCH_GEMMA_EMBEDDING2 ("gemma-embedding2")
   in llama-arch, llama_model_mapping, the models without a KV cache
   (create_memory) and the NEOX rope models (llama_model_rope_type), next to
   LLM_ARCH_GEMMA_EMBEDDING.

2. Add src/models/gemma-embedding2.cpp and its llama_model_gemma_embedding2
   in models.h: a bidirectional Gemma 4-style encoder (24 layers, hidden size
   512) with symmetric sliding window attention on five of every six layers,
   per-layer head sizes and KV heads, Q/K/V RMS norms, per-layer inputs from a
   projection only (no per-layer token embeddings), a learned output scale per
   layer, and a projection of the final hidden state to the 768-dimensional
   embedding (mean pooling, from the GGUF).

   It is upstream's file with two changes for the fork's API:
   - The fork has no llama_model_base::load_swa_pattern. The sliding window
     pattern is read as one flag per layer (as the GGUF stores it) with
     get_arr, or as a period (6 by default) with set_swa_pattern, which is
     what load_swa_pattern does upstream.
   - The fork's build_inp_embd takes no scale. The token embeddings are scaled
     by sqrt(n_embd) afterwards, only for token input, as the fork's
     gemma-embedding.cpp does.

   models/*.cpp is collected by file(GLOB) in src/CMakeLists.txt, so the new
   file needs no CMake change.

